+## Expected Outcomes
+
+When the agent uses this workflow on competitive programming problems:
+
+1. **Constraint Analysis Phase**: Agent will create notes.md listing problem constraints, compute allowed complexity, and prove algorithm fits budget. Will explicitly avoid float arithmetic on large integers and avoid BFS on huge state spaces.
+
+2. **Brute-Force Development**: Agent will write brute.py and gen.py to understand the problem through small-case exploration, deriving patterns and mathematical insights.
+
+3. **Sample Verification**: Agent will extract all samples, create test files, run with timeout, and verify every sample passes via diff before proceeding.
+
+4. **Stress Testing**: Agent will run run_tests tool with 100 random test cases, ensuring solution matches brute-force on diverse inputs.
+
+5. **Performance Validation**: Agent will generate max-size input, verify solution completes in acceptable time, and rethink algorithm (not micro-optimize) if timeout occurs.
+
+6. **Iteration**: Agent will iterate through phases until all criteria are met: samples pass, stress tests pass, and max-size input completes in time.
